# Default: normalise text in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Captured source pages are the evidence behind every licence quotation in
# README.md, and their sha256 hashes are recorded in data/manifest.json.
# Git must not touch a byte of them. Line-ending normalisation on checkout
# would change the bytes, change the hash, and silently invalidate the whole
# licence capture without anything appearing to be wrong.
sources/** -text -diff

# The sealed label artefacts are evidence in exactly the same way, and for the
# same reason git must not touch a byte of them. Hermes Cordis's set arrived from
# the vault with CRLF line endings; under the default rule above git normalised
# it on commit, so the committed blob hashed to 52e611d3… while the artefact the
# labeller sealed and posted is 2fb51176…. The content was identical after the
# conversion and the labels were unaffected, but a sealed artefact that does not
# reproduce its own hash from the repository is not evidence, it is a copy with a
# footnote. Counsel found this at cordis-sdg seq 178.
data/labels/*.json -text -diff
